%N A400135 Numbers k such that (k/p)^2 + 1 is prime for every prime factor p of k.
%C A400135 Numbers k such that A359249(k) = A001221(k).
%C A400135 Includes all primes.  All composite terms are divisible by 4.
%C A400135 Includes 4*k for k in A052291.
%H A400135 Robert Israel, <a href="/A400135/b400135.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400135 a(9) = 12 is a term because 12 has prime factors 2 and 3, and (12/2)^2 + 1 = 37 and (12/3)^2 + 1 = 17 are both prime.
%p A400135 filter:= n -> andmap(p -> isprime((n/p)^2+1), NumberTheory:-PrimeFactors(n)):
%p A400135 select(filter, [$1..1000]);
%o A400135 (Python)
%o A400135 from sympy import factorint, isprime
%o A400135 def ok(k): return all(isprime((k//p)**2 + 1) for p in factorint(k))
%o A400135 print([k for k in range(1, 240) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 20 2026
%Y A400135 Cf. A001221, A052291, A359249, A398897.
%K A400135 nonn,new
%O A400135 1,2
